.TH DOTFILES 1 "April 2026" "version 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dotfiles \- manage dotfiles with symlinks and git
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dotfiles
[\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-all\fR]
.br
.B dotfiles status
[\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-all\fR]
.br
.B dotfiles diff
[\fB\-\-staged\fR|\fB\-\-cached\fR]
[\fIname\fR ...]
.br
.B dotfiles add
[\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR]
.I path
[\fIpath\fR ...]
.br
.B dotfiles sync
[\fB\-m\fR \fImessage\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR]
.br
.B dotfiles update
[\fB\-m\fR \fImessage\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR]
.br
.B dotfiles doctor
[\fB\-\-fix\fR|\fB\-f\fR]
.br
.B dotfiles audit
[\fIpath\fR ...]
.br
.B dotfiles edit
[\fIquery\fR]
.br
.B dotfiles log
[\fB\-n\fR \fIcount\fR]
[\fIpath\fR]
.br
.B dotfiles ignore
[\fIpattern\fR ...]
.br
.B dotfiles guard
[\fIpattern\fR ...]
.br
.B dotfiles clone
.I repository
[\fIpath\fR]
.br
.B dotfiles link
[\fIname\fR ...]
.br
.B dotfiles clean
[\fIname\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dotfiles
is a CLI tool for managing dotfiles in a git repository using symlinks.
It tracks which dotfiles in the current directory are managed (symlinked into
the dotfiles repo) and which are not. Files are moved into the repo and
replaced with relative symlinks, matching the convention used by GNU Stow.
.PP
The dotfiles repository location is determined by the
.B DOTFILES_REPO_PATH
environment variable, falling back to
.IR ~/.dotfiles .
.PP
The repo structure mirrors home-relative paths: a file at
.I repo/.zshrc
maps to
.IR ~/.zshrc ,
and
.I repo/work/project/.claude
maps to
.IR ~/work/project/.claude .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B (none) [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-all\fR]
List dotfiles in the current directory, showing whether each is managed
(symlinked into the repo) or unmanaged. Unmanaged cache, runtime, and OS noise
are suppressed by default unless
.B \-a
or
.B \-\-all
is passed. When executed inside the dotfiles repository, tracked repository
files are shown directly.
.TP
.B status [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-all\fR]
Show a git-status-style view of managed dotfiles. Displays pending changes
for managed files, unpushed commits, and lists unmanaged dotfile candidates
(filtered by ignore patterns). When executed inside the dotfiles repository,
full working tree status and unpushed commits are displayed.
.TP
.B diff [\fB\-\-staged\fR|\fB\-\-cached\fR] [\fIname\fR ...]
View diff of working tree changes against the repository. If
.B \-\-staged
or
.B \-\-cached
is provided, staged changes are shown.
.TP
.B add [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR] \fIpath\fR [\fIpath\fR ...]
Move one or more files into the repo and replace them with relative
symlinks. Accepts relative paths, absolute paths, or ~/paths. Each file
must be under
.IR $HOME .
.IP
Files matching sensitive credential patterns (.ssh, .gnupg, id_rsa*, .env*,
.secrets*, *.pem, *.key) are blocked by default. Use
.B \-f
or
.B \-\-force
to override the sensitive guardrail.
.IP
If a file's real path is already inside the repo (such as a new file in a
symlinked directory like .zfuncs/), the file is staged for git without moving
or re-linking.
.TP
.B sync [\fB\-m\fR \fImessage\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR]
Pull remote updates with rebase, restore missing or new symlinks, and
commit/push any local modifications in a single operation. Scans files for
secrets before committing; use
.B \-f
or
.B \-\-force
to override.
.TP
.B update [\fB\-m\fR \fImessage\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR]
Stage, commit, pull upstream remote changes with rebase, and push changes to
managed dotfiles. When run outside the repo directory, only files managed from
the current directory are included. When run inside the repo, all changes are
included. Performs secret content checks before committing.
.TP
.B doctor [\fB\-\-fix\fR|\fB\-f\fR]
Check health of managed dotfiles, identifying clobbered symlinks (files overwritten
as regular files), missing symlinks, dangling pointers, and insecure permissions
on sensitive directories. Pass
.B \-\-fix
to automatically repair issues and backup modified local files.
.TP
.B audit [\fIpath\fR ...]
Scan managed dotfiles in the repository for credentials, private keys, AWS tokens,
GitHub PATs, Google API keys, OpenAI keys, and Slack tokens.
.TP
.B edit [\fIquery\fR]
Find and open matching managed dotfile directly in
.B $EDITOR
or
.BR $VISUAL .
Accepts fuzzy, prefix, or substring queries (e.g. zsh, alias, tmux). If no query
is given, opens the repository root directory.
.TP
.B log [\fB\-n\fR \fIcount\fR] [\fIpath\fR]
Display formatted commit history for the dotfiles repository or a specific dotfile.
.TP
.B ignore [\fIpattern\fR ...]
List current ignore patterns or append new ignore rules to
.IR ~/.dotfiles/.dotfilesignore .
.TP
.B guard [\fIpattern\fR ...]
List current sensitive guardrail patterns or append new rules to
.IR ~/.dotfiles/.dotfilesguard .
.TP
.B clone \fIrepository\fR [\fIpath\fR]
Clone a remote dotfiles repository and restore all symlinks by walking
the repo contents. The default destination is
.IR ~/.dotfiles .
.TP
.B link [\fIname\fR ...]
Restore symlinks by walking the repo contents. Creates relative symlinks
for all files in the repo, or only the specified names. Skips entries that
are already correctly linked.
.TP
.B clean [\fIname\fR ...]
Remove symlinks for managed dotfiles in the current directory and copy the
files back from the repo.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Show all dotfiles, including those ignored by built-in or custom rules.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Override sensitive guardrail checks during
.B add
or bypass secret content warnings during
.B update
and
.BR sync .
.TP
.BR \-\-fix
Automatically repair health issues identified by
.BR doctor .
.TP
.BR \-m " \fImessage\fR"
Commit message for
.B update
and
.B sync
commands.
.TP
.BR \-n " \fIcount\fR"
Number of commits to display in
.BR log .
.TP
.BR \-version ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-completion " \fIshell\fR"
Print shell completion script (zsh, bash).
.TP
.BR \-help ", " \-\-help
Display usage information.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DOTFILES_REPO_PATH
Path to the dotfiles git repository. Defaults to
.IR ~/.dotfiles .
.TP
.B EDITOR ", " VISUAL
Default text editor invoked by
.BR edit .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dotfiles doctor
Check for clobbered or broken symlinks.
.TP
.B dotfiles doctor --fix
Repair broken symlinks and backup clobbered files.
.TP
.B dotfiles audit
Scan dotfiles for leaked secrets.
.TP
.B dotfiles edit zsh
Open ~/.dotfiles/.zshrc in your configured editor.
.TP
.B dotfiles log -n 5
Show last 5 dotfiles commits with relative timestamps.
.TP
.B dotfiles diff
Show working tree differences against git repo.
.TP
.B dotfiles sync
Pull remote changes, relink, commit and push.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred.
